{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792945818,"nonce":"pvnGIbQb/wIrypQ3+oIuU8ZMuZo=","title":"Workspace interface: RayDE reads and writes files through a provider, not sys.*","message":"RayDE reaches the filesystem and processes through sys.FileSystem/sys.io.File (58 files) and sys.io.Process/Thread (8 files). Put one Workspace interface in front of them: files (list, stat, read, write, mkdir, remove, rename, watch), documents, programs (spawn, input, output, kill). Native implements it on the local filesystem and processes, unchanged in behaviour; a page implements it over the session protocol (docs/session.md). Done when no RayDE source outside the native provider calls sys.FileSystem, sys.io.File or sys.io.Process, and the existing checks pass.\n\nPart of the browser epic: git-bug ae3a156433377383faa317d5da1f34e6eab10f9a6e0d0ab0456fc0e0277a8382","files":null}]}